# API — Prisma

- Prisma client: `src/generated/prisma`. After schema change: `pnpm prisma:generate`.
- Prisma only inside **services** — not controllers.

## Filters belong in the query (locked)

Default = **Prisma `where`** on `findMany` / `count` / `findFirst` / `updateMany`. Put every list / board / search / “matches X” predicate there. Do **not** load rows then `.filter` / `if` them out in Node.

`$queryRaw` is only the fallback when Prisma cannot express the predicate (e.g. compare two columns). Still in the DB — never “fetch wide, filter in JS.”

| Bad | Why |
|-----|-----|
| `findMany({ skip, take })` then `.filter(predicate)`, `pageInfo` from leftover length | Empty pages, wrong totals, infinite scroll dies |
| Load all candidates, filter in memory for a board | Same bugs + scales poorly |
| Wide Prisma `where`, then drop rows with `if` for the response | Predicate belongs in `where` |

| OK after fetch | Why |
|----------------|-----|
| Map row → wire DTO / enrich fields | Not dropping matches |
| Tag every unit with `available` / `blockReason` (availability returns all) | Intentional full set, not a filtered page |
| Single-row guards (`if (!row)`, status transition) | Not a list filter |

`count({ where })` and `findMany({ where, skip, take })` must share the **same** Prisma `where` for paginated lists.
